{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"To access the print version of the article, a link is provided, and it seems that there is a Sudoku puzzle included. The rules of the puzzle are mostly standard, with a key exception regarding the cells contained within grey lines. These cells have a special condition that applies to them, setting them apart from the rest of the puzzle. The condition is that the numbers in these cells must add up to the figures indicated in the corner. This adds a layer of complexity to the puzzle, requiring careful consideration of the numbers and their relationships. The puzzle is a challenging and engaging activity for those who enjoy Sudoku.\n\n\n \n\nAddition to the standard Sudoku rules is made with the condition that no number can be repeated within each shape formed by grey lines. This means that each shape must contain a unique set of numbers, adding to the overall difficulty of the puzzle. The shapes formed by grey lines are a key part of the puzzle, and understanding how they interact with the numbers is crucial to solving it. The puzzle requires a combination of logical reasoning and attention to detail to complete successfully. With the special conditions in place, the puzzle offers a fun and challenging experience for those who enjoy problem-solving.\n\n\n \n\nThe Sudoku puzzle is part of the Observer Digital Edition, which can be purchased for access to the completed puzzle. This provides a convenient way for readers to check their work or to see the solution if they get stuck. The completed puzzle is a useful resource for those who want to verify their answers or learn from their mistakes. By providing the completed puzzle, the Observer Digital Edition offers a valuable tool for Sudoku enthusiasts. The puzzle itself is a great way to spend time, exercising the mind and providing entertainment.\n\n\n \n\nFor those interested in trying their hand at the puzzle, the rules and conditions are clearly explained. The standard Sudoku rules apply, with the exception of the special conditions regarding the cells contained within grey lines. The numbers in these cells must add up to the figures in the corner, and no number can be repeated within each shape. With these conditions in mind, readers can set to work on the puzzle, using their problem-solving skills to fill in the numbers. The puzzle is a great challenge, requiring a combination of logic and attention to detail.\n\n\n \n\nThe Observer Digital Edition is a great resource for those who enjoy Sudoku and other puzzles. By including the completed puzzle, it provides a useful tool for readers to check their work or learn from their mistakes. The special conditions of the puzzle, regarding the cells contained within grey lines, add a layer of complexity and challenge to the standard Sudoku rules. With its unique conditions and challenging puzzle, the Observer Digital Edition is a great way to spend time and exercise the mind. The puzzle is a fun and engaging activity, perfect for those who enjoy problem-solving and logical reasoning.\"", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"To", "logprob": -0.3599557876586914}, {"token": " access", "logprob": -0.04305403679609299}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.01105328369885683}, {"token": " print", "logprob": -0.012234875932335854}, {"token": " version", "logprob": -4.005352093372494e-05}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0024756519123911858}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.011108341626822948}, {"token": " article", "logprob": -0.4765605926513672}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.004643965046852827}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.021684227511286736}, {"token": " link", "logprob": -0.016601981595158577}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.018153591081500053}, {"token": " provided", "logprob": -0.00012361239350866526}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.0775010585784912}, {"